{"title":"Career Roadmap — Environmental Engineer","role":"Environmental Engineer","summary":"An Environmental Engineer applies engineering, chemistry, biology and environmental science to control pollution, manage industrial waste, treat water and wastewater, reduce emissions, improve resource efficiency and ensure environmental regulatory compliance.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"High — Chemical Engineering provides strong foundations in process engineering, mass/energy balances, thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, reaction engineering and industrial process control. However, students should deliberately add environmental engineering, water/wastewater treatment, pollution control and environmental regulations."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Chemical engineering + environmental fundamentals, pollution control, water treatment, laboratory and EHS exposure"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Environmental Engineer → Process/Environmental Specialist → Senior Environmental Engineer"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Environmental Manager, Sustainability Engineer, EHS/Environmental Consultant"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Environmental Director, Sustainability Head, Environmental Consultant, Climate/Decarbonisation specialist"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Chemistry, mathematics, physics, engineering fundamentals"},{"text":"Understand chemical/environmental systems"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, mass transfer, material balances"},{"text":"Understand industrial pollution sources"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Environmental engineering, water treatment, air pollution, waste management"},{"text":"Design basic treatment systems"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"EIA, environmental management, sustainability, emissions, compliance"},{"text":"Complete an industrial environmental-management project"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Scientific & Engineering Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering chemistry"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Environmental science"},{"text":"Basic programming"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"},{"text":"Laboratory safety"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Technical communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mini-project"},{"type":"p","text":"Study the environmental footprint of a chemical/industrial process:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Raw materials","Process","Energy","Emissions","Wastewater","Solid waste","Treatment","Disposal"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Chemical Engineering Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Material balances"},{"text":"Energy balances"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Mass transfer"},{"text":"Chemical reaction engineering"},{"text":"Process calculations"},{"text":"Process instrumentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"At the same time, introduce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Water chemistry"},{"text":"Environmental microbiology"},{"text":"Pollution sources"},{"text":"Industrial wastewater"},{"text":"Air emissions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a preliminary industrial wastewater treatment train:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Screening","Equalisation","Primary treatment","Biological treatment","Secondary clarification","Tertiary treatment"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Environmental Engineering Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"h","text":"Water & Wastewater"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Water quality parameters"},{"text":"BOD"},{"text":"COD"},{"text":"TSS"},{"text":"pH"},{"text":"DO"},{"text":"Activated slud